+# Epic Breakdown: Pulseboard
+
+**Project:** Pulseboard  
+**Date:** 2026-08-10  
+**Total Epics:** 3 (E000 plus 2 product epics)  
+**Estimated Total Stories:** 12–15
+
+## Epic dependency map
+
+```text
+E000 Developer Infrastructure
+          |
+          v
+E001 Protected Review Workflow
+          |
+          v
+E002 Confirmed Reminder Delivery
+```
+
+## Epic prioritization
+
+### MVP epics
+
+- E000: Developer Infrastructure
+- E001: Protected Transcript Review Workflow
+- E002: Confirmed Reminder Delivery
+
+### Enhancement epics
+
+— This four-week pilot intentionally has no enhancement epic.
+
+### Future epics
+
+— Calendar replacement, meeting recording, and autonomous outbound messaging are excluded by the product scope.
+
+## Epic definitions
+
+### E000: Developer Infrastructure
+
+**Value statement:** Establishes the test, delivery, and observability baseline that lets two engineers ship and assess the pilot safely.
+
+**Scope summary:** Configure local and CI checks for the Python API and browser UI, environment patterns, deployment path, and error reporting. It does not build user-facing Pulseboard workflow.
+
+**Success criteria:**
+
+- [ ] Lint, test, and build run locally through documented commands.
+- [ ] CI executes the same checks on proposed changes.
+- [ ] Separate development, staging, and pilot configuration exists without committed secrets.
+- [ ] Application failures and delivery failures are observable with workspace-safe context.
+
+**User stories summary:** test harness; CI/build pipeline; environment and deployment configuration; error tracking and structured logging.
+
+**Dependencies:**
+
+- **Depends on:** None.
+- **Enables:** E001 and E002.
+
+**Touch-points (creates/modifies):**
+
+- Migrations: —
+- Models/Services: —
+- Files/Components: repository test configuration, CI workflow, environment example, deployment configuration, logging/error configuration
+
+**Estimated stories:** 3–4  
+**Priority:** P0 — Foundation  
+**Target phase:** Foundation
+
+### E001: Protected Transcript Review Workflow
+
+**Value statement:** Enables facilitators to turn a workspace transcript into editable, reviewed actions while preventing any unconfirmed action from becoming delivery-ready.
+
+**Scope summary:** Deliver workspace-scoped transcript intake, action proposal extraction, and an explicit review-and-confirm flow for text, owner, and due date. It establishes the durable distinction between proposed and confirmed actions, but does not send reminders.
+
+**Success criteria:**
+
+- [ ] A facilitator can upload a transcript and receive reviewable proposed actions.
+- [ ] A facilitator can set and explicitly confirm final text, owner, and due date.
+- [ ] No unconfirmed proposal can create a delivery job or outbound action.
+- [ ] A real-role negative probe cannot read another workspace’s transcript or action.
+
+**User stories summary:** workspace access and membership; transcript upload; proposed-action extraction; proposal editing; explicit confirmation; tenant-isolation checks.
+
+**Dependencies:**
+
+- **Depends on:** E000.
+- **Enables:** E002.
+
+**Touch-points (creates/modifies):**
+
+- Migrations: workspace/membership, transcript, proposed-action, confirmed-action records
+- Models/Services: workspace access, transcript intake, extraction, action review/confirmation
+- Files/Components: browser workspace shell, transcript upload, proposal-review screen, confirmation controls
+
+**Estimated stories:** 5–6  
+**Priority:** P0 — MVP critical  
+**Target phase:** Core review
+
+### E002: Confirmed Reminder Delivery
+
+**Value statement:** Enables facilitators to complete accountable follow-through by delivering one reminder only for an explicitly confirmed action and showing its outcome.
+
+**Scope summary:** Select and configure one reminder provider, create delivery jobs only from E001’s confirmed actions, send the reminder through the provider adapter, and expose delivered or failed status. It does not add repeated campaigns, calendar replacement, or autonomous sends.
+
+**Success criteria:**
+
+- [ ] A confirmed action produces one provider-backed reminder job.
+- [ ] Delivery is never initiated from an unconfirmed proposal.
+- [ ] Facilitators can see delivered or failed status for each attempt.
+- [ ] A provider failure is visible and does not silently duplicate the reminder.
+
+**User stories summary:** provider selection/configuration; delivery job creation; provider adapter; delivery worker/retry safety; delivery-status UI; end-to-end evidence path.
+
+**Dependencies:**
+
+- **Depends on:** E000, E001, and selection of one reminder provider.
+- **Enables:** Pilot outcome measurement.
+
+**Touch-points (creates/modifies):**
+
+- Migrations: delivery-attempt/job records
+- Models/Services: delivery-job service, provider adapter, background delivery worker, delivery-status query
+- Files/Components: provider configuration, confirmed-action delivery trigger, delivery-status panel
+
+**Estimated stories:** 4–5  
+**Priority:** P0 — MVP critical  
+**Target phase:** Delivery
+
+## Execution strategy
+
+### Phase 0: Foundation
+
+**Epic:** E000.  
+**Success gate:** The team can run the pilot’s checks and inspect failures before feature work proceeds.
+
+### Phase 1: Protected review workflow
+
+**Epic:** E001.  
+**Success gate:** A facilitator can upload, review, and explicitly confirm an action in their own workspace; a cross-workspace read fails under the real request role.
+
+### Phase 2: Confirmed delivery
+
+**Epic:** E002.  
+**Success gate:** Runtime evidence covers upload → confirmation → one provider delivery with visible status.
+
+## Risks and metrics by epic
+
+| Epic | Primary risk | Mitigation | Key metric |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| E000 | Incomplete feedback loop hides regressions | Establish local and CI checks before feature work | Checks run on every proposed change |
+| E001 | Human confirmation can be bypassed or tenant scope leaks | Separate proposal/confirmed states and real-role negative test | ≥80% proposal review during pilot |
+| E002 | Provider failure creates confusion or duplicate sends | Durable jobs, idempotent provider call, visible outcome | Every attempt has delivered/failed status |
+
+## Epic concurrency waves and rebase cadence
+
+| Wave | Epics | May run in parallel? | Starts when | Daily rebase cadence |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| 0 | E000 | No | Project start | N/A — merge before E001 |
+| 1 | E001 | No | E000 is complete | N/A — E001 owns the shared workflow boundary |
+| 2 | E002 | No | E001 is complete and one provider is selected | N/A — E002 consumes confirmed actions |
+
+All epics are deliberately serial: E001 defines the confirmed-action boundary E002 must consume, and the pilot has only two engineers and a four-week time box. Before any future parallel work, update touch-points, push the planning corpus, and use the documented rebase cadence.
+
+## Notes
+
+- The plan stays within the requested maximum: two product epics plus E000.
+- Placeholder `epic.md` files are intentionally Draft, not specified. `/epic-specify` is the next lifecycle step after the recommended planning analysis.
+- Build projects with three or fewer epics are not blocked by `/project-analyze`; it remains the recommended independent planning review.
