+# Epic Specification: Confirmed Reminder Delivery
+
+**Epic ID:** E002  
+**Project:** Pulseboard  
+**Created:** 2026-08-10  
+**Status:** Planning  
+**Estimated Stories:** 4–5
+
+## Epic lifecycle state tracking
+
+**Current State**: Draft (Placeholder)
+
+- [x] **Draft** - Placeholder created by `/project-plan` (not yet specified)
+- [ ] **Specified** - epic.md created by `/epic-specify`
+- [ ] **Clarified** - Ambiguities resolved (`/epic-clarify` complete)
+- [ ] **Planned** - epic-tech-spec.md created (`/epic-plan` complete)
+- [ ] **Stories Mapped** - epic-breakdown.md created (`/epic-breakdown` complete)
+- [ ] **Validated** - Epic integration verified (`/epic-validate` complete)
+
+## Overview
+
+This placeholder reserves delivery of exactly one reminder for a facilitator-confirmed action, through a configurable provider with a visible delivered-or-failed outcome. It consumes E001’s protected confirmation boundary and does not introduce autonomous outbound messaging, campaigns, or calendar behavior.
+
+## Initial scope
+
+- Select and configure one reminder provider behind an adapter.
+- Create a delivery job only from a confirmed action.
+- Send one reminder with retry-safe, non-duplicating behavior.
+- Show delivery status to the workspace facilitator.
+
+## Dependencies
+
+- **Depends on:** E000, E001, and selection of one reminder provider.
+- **Provides to:** Pilot end-to-end evidence and follow-through outcome measurement.
+
+## Success Criteria
+
+- Confirmed actions receive one provider-backed reminder.
+- Provider outcomes are visible and failures do not silently duplicate sends.
+- End-to-end runtime evidence can exercise upload through delivery.
+
